# SPA fallback: this is a client-side-routed React app (react-router), so any
# path that isn't a real static file has to still serve index.html and let
# the router take over — otherwise a reload or a link opened in a new tab on
# any route but "/" 404s at the host instead of reaching React at all.
# Netlify and Cloudflare Pages both read this exact file/syntax; see
# vercel.json for the equivalent rule if the project ever serves from Vercel.
/*    /index.html   200
